Defects found:

- **Line 88 / off-by-one primary selection**  
  Input: `primaryOutcomes=[{"measure":"Recurrent VTE","description":""},{"measure":"Composite of Venous Thrombotic Event or Major Bleeding","description":""}]`.  
  Consequence: P45 reads only `primaryOutcomes[0]`, so a fused second registered primary is never tested.

- **Line 185 with line 246 / ZERO CONFLATED WITH ABSENT**  
  Input: `assess_reading("X", [{"nct":"A","state":"READ","comparator_families_present":[],"registered_primary_title":"Recurrent VTE","registered_primary_description_verbatim":""},{"nct":"B","state":"READ","comparator_families_present":[],"registered_primary_title":"Recurrent VTE","registered_primary_description_verbatim":""}])`.  
  Consequence: an absent/unread comparator family becomes `len(fams)==0`, producing `NO_BARRIER_FOUND_BY_THESE_THREE_TESTS`.

- **Line 143 / NEGATION DROPPED**  
  Input: `fuses_efficacy_and_safety({"registered_primary_title":"Recurrent VTE, not Major Bleeding","registered_primary_description_verbatim":""})`.  
  Consequence: the title explicitly excludes bleeding, but substring matching sets both limbs true and fires P45.

- **Line 107 with line 136 / SELECTOR KEYED TO TOO-NARROW FORM**  
  Input: `fuses_efficacy_and_safety({"registered_primary_title":"DVT or Major Bleeding","registered_primary_description_verbatim":""})`.  
  Consequence: `" dvt"` misses DVT at start of title, so a fused thrombotic-plus-bleeding endpoint is not detected.

- **Lines 309-314 / check cannot fail, instrument reads assertion not corpus**  
  Input: `scr={"rows":[{"nct":"NCT00329238","reading":"TREATMENT"},{"nct":"NCT02913326","reading":"TREATMENT"},{"nct":"NCT00168805","reading":"TREATMENT"},{"nct":"NCT01505881","reading":"TREATMENT"}]}`.  
  Consequence: `readings_spanned` still uses `OBJECT_TRIALS` declarations and reports three readings even when the screened corpus says otherwise.

